Package: tidydiversity
Title: Tidy Biodiversity Estimation with Hill Numbers
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: 
    person("Jimmy", "Moses", , "jimmy.moses@pnguot.ac.pg", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Tidy, pipe-friendly tools for estimating biodiversity from
    long-format community data. Computes Hill numbers, asymptotic diversity
    estimates, sample coverage, size- and coverage-based rarefaction and
    extrapolation following Chao et al. (2014) <doi:10.1890/13-0133.1>, and
    partitions beta diversity into turnover and nestedness components
    following Baselga (2010) <doi:10.1111/j.1466-8238.2009.00490.x>. Every
    function takes a data frame and returns a tibble, uses data-masking for
    column arguments, and supports grouped data and the '.by' argument.
